# Python project files
# NOTE: python-bridge/poetry.lock IS committed (like qontinui-web/backend's):
# the runner's dev-service build_command and the supervisor build pool run bare
# `poetry install`, which hard-fails when a local lock goes stale against a
# changed pyproject. Committing the lock keeps every machine's provisioning
# deterministic. Regenerate with `poetry lock` on dependency changes.
python-bridge/tox.ini
python-bridge/requirements.txt

# Optional config files (add when ready)
docs/TESTING_CHECKLIST.md
python-bridge/test_*.py
test_python_executor.sh
python-bridge/test_full_communication.py
# Ignore docs/ contents (use docs/* not docs/ so a single file can be
# re-included — git can't re-include under an excluded *directory*).
docs/*
# ...but the generated runner onboarding checklist IS tracked (Phase-5
# anti-drift gate diffs it against a fresh `coord_doctor --onboarding-doc`).
!docs/runner-onboarding.md
# ...and so is the generated config-layer inventory, for the same reason: it is
# the published output of `config_report --layer-doc`, held byte-exact by
# `config_report::tests::config_report_checked_in_layer_doc_is_the_generators_output`.
!docs/runner-config-layers.md
# ...and so is the generated capability roster: it is the published output of
# `qontinui-runner --capability-manifest-doc`, held byte-exact by
# `headless_manifest_tests::the_checked_in_capability_doc_matches_a_fresh_render`
# and by `.github/workflows/capability-manifest-fresh.yml`. A gate that diffs a
# file git does not carry gates nothing.
!docs/runner-capabilities.md
# Same local-only documentation convention applies to nested docs/ dirs.
python-bridge/docs/*

# Configuration files
configs/
demo-config.json
*_config.json
debugger_config.json

# Build/config files
postcss.config.js
tailwind.config.js
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.node.json
vite.config.ts

# Icon source files (for packaging only, platform-specific)
icons/source/

# Development/diagnostic files
python-bridge/diagnostics/
temp_dev/
# .qontinui runtime-state dirs stay ignored, but the CI manifest is
# REPO CONTENT (runner-as-CI-node lane reads .qontinui/ci.toml from the
# checked-out tree) — `dir/*` + negation, because a fully-ignored dir
# (`.qontinui/`) can never have children re-included.
.qontinui/*
!.qontinui/ci.toml

# Ignore CLAUDE notes file
CLAUDE.md
python-bridge/build/
python-bridge/dist/

# Bundled Python executors (large, platform-specific)
